        "Content": "\n23/10/2026 - 12:00\n\nFOR SALE BY LIVE STREAM PROPERTY AUCTION, FRIDAY 23RD OCTOBER AT 12.00 NOON.\n\nYou Must Pre-Register on Our Website by Thursday 22ND to bid.\n\nO'Donnellan & Joyce Auctioneers are delighted to offer for sale by auction this spacious five-bedroom end-of-terrace property, ideally positioned at 1 Quinn Terrace, Mervue, Galway.\n\nSituated on the east side of Galway City, no. 1 Quinn Avenue has been vacant since February 2024 and so should qualifty for the for Vacancy Grants\n\nQuinn Avenue is a established and highly convenient residential location, offering the perfect balance of easy access to the city centre and the many benefits of suburban living. \n\nThe area is well served by an excellent range of sporting, recreational, educational and commercial amenities, making it an attractive choice for homeowners and investors alike.\n\nThe property is located within easy reach of a number of schools and educational facilities, including Mervue Primary School, Radharc na Mara National School and Galway Community College. ATU's Creative Arts and Media campus on Wellpark Road is also located close by, providing excellent accessibility for students and staff.\n\nThe accommodation is well proportioned and comprises an entrance hall, living room, kitchen, dining room, office/bedroom, utility room and bathroom at ground-floor level. Upstairs, there are five further bedrooms, providing generous accommodation and excellent flexibility for family living, home working or investment purposes.\n\nThe property also benefits from its proximity to Liosbán and Mervue Industrial Estate, providing easy access to a wide range of retail, commercial and employment opportunities. Galway's renowned medical and medtech sector is also close at hand, with major employers and healthcare facilities including Merlin Park Hospital, Bon Secours Private Hospital, Galway Clinic, Boston Scientific, Merit Medical and Creganna all located within the wider area.\n\nFor commuters, the property enjoys convenient access to the M6 and M18 motorway networks, providing excellent transport links to Galway, Dublin, Limerick and beyond.\n\nWith its generous bedroom accommodation, convenient location and strong proximity to employment, education and transport links, 1 Quinn Terrace represents an excellent opportunity for a first-time buyer, family or investor.\n\nViewing is highly recommended and is sure to impress.\n\nSOLICITOR WITH CARRIAGE OF SALE: Ms. Jenny Prendegast, Cleggan House, 46 Eyre Square, Galway, H91 Y3X6.\n\n\nAUCTION PROCESS \nPre-Registration Required in Order to Bid By Phone or Online. Please familiarize yourself with the Auction Process prior to bidding.\n\nPlease note the following:\n\n5,000 bidder security fee must be paid in advance to bid on the day (if unsuccessful this is fully refunded to you) If you are successful, you are immediately contracted on the drop of the hammer and the non-refundable balance of 10% must be paid immediately. \n\nPhone and Online bidding service available you must pre-register to bid prior to Auction Day - you can register on our website under the auction tab at top of the homepage. \n\n\nRegister for legals on our website under the auction tab at top of the homepage (please note all legals may not be available for download until closer to the auction date - once you have registered you will receive an alert when they do become available). We always advise potential purchasers to have their solicitor review legals prior to bidding.\n\n\nNOTE: These particulars are not to be considered a formal offer. They are for information only and give a general idea of the property. They are not to be taken as forming any part of a resulting contract, nor to be relied upon as statements or representations of fact. \n\nFLOORPLANS: The floor plan including furniture, fixture measurements and dimensions are approximate and for illustrative purposes only. The Polycam App used gives no guarantee, warranty or representation as to the accuracy and layout. All enquiries must be directed to the agent.\n\nWhilst every care is taken in their preparation, neither O'Donnellan & Joyce Auctioneers nor the vendor accept any liability as to their accuracy. Intending purchasers must satisfy themselves by personal inspection or otherwise as to the correctness of these particulars.\n\nNo person in the employment of O'Donnellan & Joyce Auctioneers has any authority to make or give any representation or warranty whatever in relation to this property.\n\nNote: Prospective purchasers must satisfy themselves as to the condition and suitability of the property, its existing or potential use, any development or redevelopment potential, any necessary planning permissions or other consents, and as to the availability of and eligibility of the property and/or any prospective purchaser for any grants, schemes or funding. No representation or warranty is made or given by or on behalf of the Vendor in relation to any such matters."
      },
